    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first Sabinsville post office opened in 1849 during President Zachary Taylor’s term, with Douglass also building the town’s first sawmill and hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
