      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Maple sugaring peaked in Sabinsville in 1870, producing over 145,000 pounds that were shipped down the Cowanesque River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sabinsville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sabinsville sits where the east and west branches of Mill Creek meet, just a stone’s throw from the New York state line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
